	(footprint "RaspberryPi_Pico_SMD_or_THT_Debug"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "21ebefef-d1bc-4cd6-b973-0b7113e329d6")
		(at 143 106 90)
		(descr "Raspberry Pi Pico 2 (non-W), solderable EITHER WAY: KiCad's own Module:RaspberryPi_Pico_SMD_HandSolder -- pads, silk, courtyard and 3D model vendored unchanged, including its D1/D2/D3 debug pads -- plus a through-hole at every pin, so the same board takes a reflowed/castellation-soldered module or a socketed one on 2.54 mm headers (owner call, #1062). The holes are KiCad's own THT positions (Module:RaspberryPi_Pico_Common_THT, pins at +/-8.89 from the centre line) shifted into this footprint's centred frame; they sit 0.8 mm inboard of the hand-solder pads and share their pad numbers, so each pin is one landing area with a hole in it. The three debug holes land exactly on D1/D2/D3, which the plain Pico 2 carries as 0.1 in through-holes -- SWD stays on the board either way. The Pico W antenna keep-out that the shared THT footprint carries is deliberately NOT here: this is the non-W part, and that zone sits exactly over the debug pads.")
		(tags "module usb pcb swd")
